# Monotonicity of the number of index-`ℓ` subgroups under a prime-index inclusion

Let `V ≤ W` be additive subgroups of an abelian group `G` with `V` of relative index a
prime `p` in `W`.  Then the number of additive subgroups of index `ℓ` of `V` is at most
the number of those of `W`.  In the vocabulary of `NK.LocalCFT.Units.EllRank.Defs`, the
number of index-`ℓ` subgroups of `A` is the number of points of the projective space of
the dual of the elementary abelian quotient `A ⧸ ℓA`
(`NK.LocalCFT.Units.EllRank.nIdx_eq_natCard_projectivization`), so the statement proved
here is

`Nat.card (ℙ (ZMod ℓ) (ellDual ℓ ↥V)) ≤ Nat.card (ℙ (ZMod ℓ) (ellDual ℓ ↥W))`.

The proof reduces this to the corresponding inequality of dimensions of the `𝔽_ℓ`-vector
spaces `V ⧸ ℓV` and `W ⧸ ℓW`, using `Projectivization.card_of_finrank`, and the dimension
inequality is proved by two different arguments:

* if `ℓ ≠ p`, the natural map `V ⧸ ℓV → W ⧸ ℓW` is an isomorphism.  Injectivity and
  surjectivity both follow from a Bézout identity `A * ℓ + B * p = 1` together with
  `p • w ∈ V` for `w ∈ W` (`nsmul_mem_of_relIndex_prime`), which is available because
  `W ⧸ V` has order `p`;

* if `ℓ = p`, the maps `φ : V ⧸ pV → W ⧸ pW` (induced by the inclusion) and
  `ψ : W ⧸ pW → V ⧸ pV` (`x ↦ p • x`, well defined since `p • W ≤ V`) satisfy
  `range ψ = ker φ` and `range φ ≤ ker ψ`.  The rank-nullity theorem for `φ` and `ψ`
  therefore gives `rank (V ⧸ pV) ≤ rank (W ⧸ pW)`.  Moreover `W ⧸ V ≅ 𝔽_p` is generated by
  a single element (`exists_sub_mem_of_relIndex_prime`), whence the cokernel of `φ` is at
  most one-dimensional; this is what transfers finiteness of the dimension from `V ⧸ pV`
  to `W ⧸ pW`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.LocalCFT.Units.EllRank.Defs
import Submission.NK.LocalCFT.Units.EllRank.natCard_projectivization_le_of_finrank_le
import Submission.NK.LocalCFT.Units.EllRank.exists_sub_mem_of_relIndex_prime
import Submission.NK.LocalCFT.Units.EllRank.nsmul_mem_of_relIndex_prime
